From a5196862eefbd37800ccece9ec4d40dea5ee660c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Maxime=20M=C3=A9r=C3=A9?= <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Date: Tue, 2 Jun 2026 18:18:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 472/572] fix(st-ddr): do not panic on ddrphy_init error during
 self-refresh exit
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

During standby exit (self-refresh path), stm32mp1_ddrphy_init() is
expected to return -EINVAL because ZQ calibration is bypassed
(DDRPHYC_PIR_ZCALBYP), so ZQ0SRN_ZDONE is not set. The proper ZQ
calibration is performed afterward by stm32mp1_self_refresh_zcal().

A rebase introduced an early error check after stm32mp1_ddrphy_init()
that causes a panic before reaching stm32mp1_self_refresh_zcal(),
breaking standby resume.

Restore the original error handling: defer the panic check until after
stm32mp1_self_refresh_zcal() has been called in the self-refresh case.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/arm-trusted-firmware.git d502b352385e01f781f4fd675b64c2bb021f2b93 fix(st-ddr): do not panic on ddrphy_init error during self-refresh exit]
Change-Id: If902456fa31778883cc26129ab7b2cf1584cad73
Signed-off-by: Maxime Méré <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/tf-a/+/573891
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
Domain-Review: Nicolas LE BAYON <nicolas.le.bayon@st.com>
Reviewed-by: Nicolas LE BAYON <nicolas.le.bayon@st.com>
---
 drivers/st/ddr/stm32mp1_ddr.c | 10 ++++------
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/st/ddr/stm32mp1_ddr.c b/drivers/st/ddr/stm32mp1_ddr.c
index f4f037247e..345337e4ca 100644
--- a/drivers/st/ddr/stm32mp1_ddr.c
+++ b/drivers/st/ddr/stm32mp1_ddr.c
@@ -845,16 +845,14 @@ void stm32mp1_ddr_init(struct stm32mp_ddr_priv *priv,
 	}
 
 	ret = stm32mp1_ddrphy_init(priv->phy, pir);
-	if (ret != 0) {
-		panic();
-	}
 
 	if (config->self_refresh) {
 		/* Re-init PHY with ZQ calibration */
 		ret = stm32mp1_self_refresh_zcal(priv, config->zdata);
-		if (ret != 0) {
-			panic();
-		}
+	}
+
+	if (ret != 0) {
+		panic();
 	}
 
 	/*
